      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T21:17:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I reproduced this with snapd 2.78’s configuration transaction code and in-memory state. After seeding `ceph.demo` with a pool, monitors, user and key, applying `{\"ceph.demo\": {\"fsid\": \"test-fsid\"}}` left only the FSID. Applying `{\"ceph.demo.fsid\": \"test-fsid\"}` preserved all four settings. This helper sends the first form.\n\nIf the FSID-only write succeeds, the `NOT_RENDERED` retry reads the incomplete settings and `ceph-check` returns `USAGE`. Can we patch the FSID leaf directly or resend the complete backend config? The settings test helper merges the mocked writes, and the retry test supplies `OK` without reading the new settings.\n\nhttps://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/00b63144e44cdb7bd059e40e947e720b942c55ec/overlord/configstate/config/transaction.go#L415-L431\nhttps://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/sunbeam-charms/+/1009341/11/charms/storage/cinder-volume-ceph/tests/unit/test_cinder_volume_ceph_scenario.py#142\nhttps://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/sunbeam-charms/+/1009341/11/charms/storage/cinder-volume-ceph/tests/unit/test_cinder_volume_ceph_scenario.py#562",
      "revId": "8eaf099978cd7f3a7f48ccf2aefa923096aa4257",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
